{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return rule","requirement":"A lessor may not require more than one month's rent as a security deposit, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% annual interest, and return it with an itemized list of damages within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent deposit; 5% interest per year; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"All residential real property leases in Massachusetts; applies to lessors, their agents and successors in interest.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential real property leases"},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest liability for the deposit does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"Lessor forfeits the right to retain any portion of the deposit or to counterclaim; failure to hold or return it gives treble the deposit or balance plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2);","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on upfront tenant payments","requirement":"At or before a tenancy begins, a lessor or agent may not require payment beyond first month's rent, last month's rent, a one-month security deposit and key/lock costs; an optional fee in lieu of a deposit may not exceed one month's rent.","key_value":"First month's rent + last month's rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key/lock cost; fee in lieu of deposit max 1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in Massachusetts; applies to lessors and their agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential tenancies"},"exemptions":"A fee in lieu of a security deposit, authorized by regulations of the executive office of housing and livable communities, may replace the deposit and is optional for both tenant and lessor.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":true,"conflict_note":"Packet shows two versions of clause (1)(b), one effective until August 1, 2025 and the 2025, 9 amendment effective August 1, 2025, which is used here."}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit offering limit","requirement":"A lessor offering a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every prospective tenant whose application is approved, regardless of income or credit score, and may not consider income or credit score in setting the fee amount.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit under regulations of the executive office of housing and livable communities, for all prospective tenants whose applications are approved.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Lessors offering a fee in lieu of a security deposit"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(E) require a lessor who offers such a fee in lieu of security deposit:  (I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.6,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
